<pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I506f35398584b4f8083bf5728ed06fdbbe84feeb" commit="3fad450eb61baf5a611474dcc24e562d1f01ac31" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm/nouveau/mmu/gk20a: program PDE through CPU  When creating new channel, the page directory initialization of fifo context takes around 80ms because we program PDE through PRAMIN. This is fine generally, but in some extreme test cases like having multiple threads which create and destroy channels 100 times, the slow PDE programming becomes the bottleneck. So to speed up the channel creation, we program PDE by CPU.  Change-Id: I506f35398584b4f8083bf5728ed06fdbbe84feeb Signed-off-by: Vince Hsu &lt;vince.h@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/340905 Commit-Ready: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Tony Zlatinski &lt;tzlatinski@nvidia.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="340905" owner_email="vince.h@nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/05/340905/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Iae6f077d180541a5b56617718579838e0a33d7c7" commit="fff7792be7b28a9fe3be648f404223f4bdbb2193" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm/nouveau/gr/gf100: speed up GR context creation  When allocating context we don't necessarily initialize the memory as zeros because the initialization will be done later in the same function. Removing the flag NVOBJ_FLAG_ZERO_ALLOC can reduce the GR context creation time significantly.  Change-Id: Iae6f077d180541a5b56617718579838e0a33d7c7 Signed-off-by: Vince Hsu &lt;vince.h@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/341831 Commit-Ready: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Stéphan